{
  "description": "Alarm engine scenarios shared by electron/src/engine-vectors.test.ts and android/app/src/test/java/com/yassine/alarmcalendar/engine/SharedVectorsTest.kt. Time is a fake clock starting at `start`; the list is pushed at `start` and again for a step with `push`. Events A, B and C stand for the uuids under `events`. A step sets the clock to `at` (running every wake-up on the way, like timers or AlarmManager would), pushes a new list if it has `push`, performs `action` (done, snooze or close, for `event`), then checks `ringing` (alarms on screen, compared as a set) and `pending` (completions made here and not drained: event, occurrence instant, snoozes used). `snoozesLeft` is the number of snoozes still offered, `snoozeLabel` the exact button text (null when there is no button) and `noticeShown` whether 'No snoozes left, do it now' is shown.",
